  "about": "How much a page carries, as numbers. The check reads every bound from the preset the deck was built in; the builder reads the build numbers of the same preset. Sizes are points on a 960 x 540 page. Sparse is a deck a speaker stands beside, Full is a deck read at a desk, Standard sits between. The fill bounds are set from this pack's own renders with a margin of 0.02: across three invented decks the content pages measure 0.29 to 0.65 of the body in Standard (lower half from 0.19) and 0.16 to 0.59 in Sparse (lower half from 0.14), and a closing page 0.20 to 0.29 in Standard and 0.24 to 0.40 in Sparse. On the printed pages of the PDF the same decks and two more measure from 0.28 in Standard (lower half from 0.21) and from 0.19 in Sparse (lower half from 0.18), a closing page from 0.20 and 0.24: inside the same bounds, which stand. Published consulting decks measure about 0.8 on a looser count; the guideline has those figures.",
